# Executive Summary

Sprint 04 successfully implemented the core security and identity capabilities for the WarehousePro Azure Landing Zone using modular Azure Bicep Infrastructure as Code.

The objective of this sprint was to secure the existing Azure Landing Zone through layered network security, centralized firewall inspection, secure administrative access, private connectivity, secure secret management and managed identity authentication.

During implementation several security improvements were introduced. Network Security Groups were implemented across the regional warehouse environments, Azure Firewall was deployed within the central hub, Azure Bastion was introduced for secure administrative access, and Private Endpoint connectivity was implemented for Azure Key Vault.

Azure Key Vault was deployed with RBAC authorization, soft delete, purge protection and public network access disabled. A user-assigned Managed Identity was also deployed and configured for secure Azure resource authentication without requiring stored credentials.

Security validation was performed across the deployed infrastructure. NSGs, security rules, route tables, Azure Firewall, Azure Bastion, Key Vault, Private Endpoint connectivity, Managed Identity and RBAC configuration were validated successfully.

All planned Sprint 04 security capabilities were implemented, validated, documented and prepared for continuation into the next sprint.

